### Application 2: Real-Time IoT Sensor Data Processing & Monitoring

**Business Context:**
A manufacturing company has 10,000+ IoT sensors monitoring temperature, pressure, humidity, and vibration across production facilities. Needs real-time monitoring, anomaly detection, and predictive maintenance.

**Problem Statement:**
- Process 1 million+ sensor readings per minute
- Real-time alerting for anomalies
- Predict equipment failures before they happen
- Dashboard showing live facility status
- Historical analysis for patterns

**Theory & Approach:**
- Use Structured Streaming for real-time micro-batch processing
- Separate hot path (alerts) from cold path (storage)
- Maintain windowed aggregations for trend detection
- Apply statistical process control for anomaly detection
- Use watermarks to handle late-arriving data

**Implementation:**

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
from pyspark.sql.functions import (
    col, avg, stddev, max, min, window, 
    when, expr, broadcast
)
from pyspark.sql.types import StructType, StructField, StringType, DoubleType, LongType

spark = SparkSession.builder \
    .appName("IoT Sensor Stream Processing") \
    .config("spark.sql.streaming.checkpointLocation", "/tmp/checkpoint") \
    .getOrCreate()

# ===== DEFINE SENSOR DATA SCHEMA =====
sensor_schema = StructType([
    StructField("sensor_id", StringType(), True),
    StructField("facility_id", StringType(), True),
    StructField("sensor_type", StringType(), True),  # temperature, pressure, humidity, vibration
    StructField("value", DoubleType(), True),
    StructField("timestamp", LongType(), True),
    StructField("unit", StringType(), True)
])

# ===== READ STREAMING DATA FROM KAFKA =====
sensor_stream = spark.readStream \
    .format("kafka") \
    .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", "localhost:9092") \
    .option("subscribe", "iot-sensors") \
    .option("startingOffsets", "latest") \
    .load() \
    .select(from_json(col("value").cast("string"), sensor_schema).alias("data")) \
    .select("data.*") \
    .withColumn("event_time", from_unixtime(col("timestamp")))

# ===== LOAD SENSOR CONFIGURATION & THRESHOLDS =====
# Static configuration for normal operating ranges
sensor_config = spark.read.parquet("/data/sensor_config")
# Contains: sensor_id, min_normal, max_normal, alert_threshold, expected_value

config_broadcast = broadcast(sensor_config)

# ===== ENRICH STREAM WITH CONFIGURATION =====
enriched_stream = sensor_stream \
    .join(config_broadcast, "sensor_id", "left") \
    .select(
        col("sensor_id"),
        col("facility_id"),
        col("sensor_type"),
        col("value"),
        col("event_time"),
        col("unit"),
        col("min_normal"),
        col("max_normal"),
        col("alert_threshold")
    )

# ===== REAL-TIME ANOMALY DETECTION =====
# Detect immediate anomalies (out of range)
anomalies_stream = enriched_stream \
    .withColumn(
        "is_anomaly",
        when(
            (col("value") < col("min_normal")) | (col("value") > col("max_normal")),
            True
        ).otherwise(False)
    ) \
    .filter(col("is_anomaly") == True) \
    .select(
        col("sensor_id"),
        col("facility_id"),
        col("sensor_type"),
        col("value"),
        col("event_time"),
        lit("OUT_OF_RANGE").alias("anomaly_type")
    )

# ===== WINDOWED STATISTICS FOR TREND DETECTION =====
# 5-minute tumbling window with 30-second slide
windowed_stats = enriched_stream \
    .withWatermark("event_time", "10 minutes") \
    .groupBy(
        window(col("event_time"), "5 minutes", "30 seconds"),
        col("sensor_id"),
        col("facility_id"),
        col("sensor_type")
    ) \
    .agg(
        avg("value").alias("avg_value"),
        stddev("value").alias("stddev_value"),
        min("value").alias("min_value"),
        max("value").alias("max_value"),
        count("*").alias("reading_count")
    ) \
    .withColumn(
        "trend_anomaly",
        when(col("stddev_value") > 5.0, True).otherwise(False)
    )

# ===== ALERT GENERATION STREAM =====
alerts_stream = anomalies_stream \
    .union(
        windowed_stats.filter(col("trend_anomaly") == True)
            .select(
                col("sensor_id"),
                col("facility_id"),
                col("sensor_type"),
                col("avg_value").alias("value"),
                col("window").cast("string").alias("event_time"),
                lit("TREND_ANOMALY").alias("anomaly_type")
            )
    ) \
    .withColumn("alert_timestamp", current_timestamp())

# ===== OUTPUT 1: REAL-TIME ALERTS TO CONSOLE (for monitoring) =====
alert_query = alerts_stream \
    .writeStream \
    .format("console") \
    .option("checkpointLocation", "/tmp/alerts_checkpoint") \
    .option("numRows", 50) \
    .start()

# ===== OUTPUT 2: WRITE ALERTS TO KAFKA TOPIC (for external systems) =====
alert_kafka_query = alerts_stream \
    .select(to_json(struct("*")).alias("value")) \
    .writeStream \
    .format("kafka") \
    .option("kafka.bootstrap.servers", "localhost:9092") \
    .option("topic", "sensor-alerts") \
    .option("checkpointLocation", "/tmp/kafka_alerts_checkpoint") \
    .start()

# ===== OUTPUT 3: PERSIST STATISTICS FOR ANALYTICS =====
stats_query = windowed_stats \
    .writeStream \
    .format("parquet") \
    .option("path", "/data/sensor_statistics") \
    .option("checkpointLocation", "/tmp/stats_checkpoint") \
    .partitionBy("facility_id", "sensor_type") \
    .start()

# ===== OUTPUT 4: LIVE DASHBOARD DATA (Append mode) =====
dashboard_stream = windowed_stats \
    .select(
        col("sensor_id"),
        col("facility_id"),
        col("sensor_type"),
        col("avg_value"),
        col("max_value"),
        col("min_value"),
        col("reading_count"),
        col("window").cast("string").alias("time_window")
    )

dashboard_query = dashboard_stream \
    .writeStream \
    .format("memory") \
    .option("checkpointLocation", "/tmp/dashboard_checkpoint") \
    .queryName("dashboard_stats") \
    .start()

# ===== BATCH QUERY ON STREAMING DATA (Ad-hoc analysis) =====
# Can query live dashboard data
spark.sql("SELECT * FROM dashboard_stats WHERE facility_id = 'FACILITY_001'").show()

# ===== WAIT FOR TERMINATION =====
spark.streams.awaitAnyTermination()
```

**Key Insights:**
- Watermarking handles late-arriving sensor data gracefully
- Windowed aggregations detect trends in addition to point anomalies
- Multiple output sinks (console, Kafka, storage, memory) serve different purposes
- Broadcasting static configuration reduces memory footprint
- Real-time processing enables immediate alerting

